# prism-coder:9b — pin num_ctx, and NOTHING else
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# WHY THIS EXISTS
#
# The 2026-08-14 vision push republished prism-coder:9b with its SYSTEM line and
# all four PARAMETER lines dropped. Confirm with:
#
#     ollama show --modelfile prism-coder:9b                      # TEMPLATE only
#     ollama show --modelfile dcostenco/prism-coder:9b-textonly-backup
#
# 4b and 2b survived the same push intact, so this is a 9b-only packaging
# regression: the weights are fine, the manifest is not.
#
# WHY IT DOES NOT SIMPLY RESTORE THE BACKUP
#
# The obvious move — copy the four PARAMETER lines and the SYSTEM line back from
# the backup — is measurably WRONG. Isolated 2026-08-16 on the executed-code
# suite (temperature 0, verified deterministic over 3 runs each, comparing
# SHA-256 of the generated source):
#
#   prism-coder:9b            (stock)             semver PASS   hash 3fd3e65e
#   + PARAMETER num_ctx only                      semver PASS   hash 3fd3e65e  <- identical
#   + SYSTEM line only                            semver FAIL   hash 8f87b3ee
#   + SYSTEM and all backup PARAMETERs            semver FAIL   hash 8f87b3ee
#
# The SYSTEM line alone flips the result. Ollama injects it even though
# TEMPLATE is a bare `{{ .Prompt }}` passthrough with no {{ .System }}
# placeholder, and prism already builds its own full prompt — so the Modelfile
# SYSTEM is a second, conflicting instruction written for the pre-vision
# text-only weights. Restoring it costs accuracy for nothing.
#
# num_ctx is byte-identical to stock, so pinning it is free. That is the whole
# change: make the context explicit instead of inheriting whatever default the
# installed Ollama happens to use. TEMPLATE {{ .Prompt }} is deliberate and
# matches 4b/2b. temperature is passed per-request by prism, not baked here.
#
# Measured KV cost of the 32768 pin on this host: 6.3 -> 6.9 GB resident
# (`ollama ps`), well inside the tier's 9 GB minFreeGb gate.
#
# AFTER ADOPTING THIS, and only after, modelPicker.ts MODEL_TIERS may raise the
# 9b ctxTokens from 4_096 to 32_768. Raising it first would be fail-open: on a
# host still inheriting a smaller default, an oversize prompt is truncated
# silently, which is exactly what the §5.4 ctx gate exists to prevent.
#
# Build a candidate (safe — leaves the live tag alone):
#   ollama create prism-coder:9b-fixed -f scripts/prism-coder-9b.Modelfile
# Adopt (OVERWRITES the live tag; other agents on this machine share the
# registry, so do this deliberately, not incidentally):
#   ollama create prism-coder:9b -f scripts/prism-coder-9b.Modelfile

FROM prism-coder:9b

TEMPLATE {{ .Prompt }}

PARAMETER num_ctx 32768
